---
export const prerender = true;
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="About CrawlPact | CrawlPact"
  description="What CrawlPact is, how it evaluates AI crawler policy, and the principles behind it."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-h1 text-neutral-950">About CrawlPact</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact audits and monitors what a website's own declared signals — <code>robots.txt</code>,
      meta robots tags, <code>X-Robots-Tag</code> headers, <code>llms.txt</code>, RSL, and Content
      Signals — say about AI crawler access, and reports that honestly against a versioned,
      source-backed registry of documented AI crawlers.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-h3 text-neutral-950">What CrawlPact is not</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      CrawlPact does not use an AI model to produce its results. Every finding traces to a
      deterministic parser and rules engine evaluating your site's own declared files against a
      registry entry with a cited official source — see <a
        href="/methodology"
        class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">methodology</a
      >. CrawlPact also does not modify your website, and it does not guarantee that any crawler
      obeys a declared instruction — see <a
        href="/limitations"
        class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">limitations</a
      > for what a result can and cannot prove.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-h3 text-neutral-950">Principles</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-body text-neutral-700">
      <li>
        <strong>Vendor neutral.</strong> The crawler registry is built from each operator's own published
        documentation, not any single operator's product interests.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Evidence based.</strong> Every finding cites the specific matched rule, line number, and
        source behind it — not a summary judgement without a trail back to the evidence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Honest about uncertainty.</strong> A crawler CrawlPact cannot verify against an official
        source is marked unverified, not guessed. An unimplemented or disabled feature says so, rather
        than fabricating a result.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-h3 text-neutral-950">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-body text-neutral-700">
      See <a href="/security" class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">security</a>,
      <a href="/privacy" class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">privacy</a>, and
      <a href="/status" class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">status</a> for operational
      details, or run a
      <a href="/audit" class="text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-2">free audit</a> to see the methodology
      applied to a real domain.
    </p>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
